From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a finger on a window is the window's

A touch on <app> went to the page's touch-action, which is auto: a drag
over a native window panned the shell, or ended in a pointercancel
before the client heard it. <app> is now `touch-action: none` in the UA
stylesheet, so every touch point reaches HTMLAppElement::ForwardTouch,
which hands it to the client as `wl_touch`.

A shell can still set its own touch-action on an <app>.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css
index 8a7ac1c..0bb115a 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css
@@ -1907,7 +1907,11 @@ iframe {
    way an <img> does; neither gets a border, because a shell draws its own
    chrome and a default frame border would be inside the window. */
 app {
-    display: inline-block
+    display: inline-block;
+    /* A finger on a window is the window's: the page does not pan or zoom
+       under it, so the client gets every touch point (HTMLAppElement::
+       ForwardTouch). */
+    touch-action: none
 }
 
 webview {
